WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.005
The expertise reversal effect describes a common instructional design problem: support that helps beginners may become unnecessary or inefficient for more advanced learners.

2
00:00:10.005 --> 00:00:15.225
A novice may need a worked example with step-by-step explanation.

3
00:00:15.225 --> 00:00:26.100
An experienced learner may find the same explanation slow, repetitive, or distracting because they already have the schema that the support is trying to build.

4
00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:28.710
Prior knowledge changes the design need.

5
00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:33.060
Beginners benefit from more guidance, clearer sequencing, and reduced search.

6
00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:38.716
Intermediate learners may need partially faded examples, targeted practice, and feedback on judgment.

7
00:00:38.716 --> 00:00:46.111
Advanced learners may need realistic cases, edge conditions, and optional references rather than mandatory explanations of basics.

8
00:00:46.111 --> 00:00:50.461
One design does not serve every learner equally well forever.

9
00:00:50.461 --> 00:00:52.636
Adaptive design can be simple.

10
00:00:52.636 --> 00:00:53.941
Offer optional guidance.

11
00:00:53.941 --> 00:00:56.986
Let learners reveal hints only when needed.

12
00:00:56.986 --> 00:01:01.771
Provide quick refreshers instead of forcing everyone through a long explanation.

13
00:01:01.771 --> 00:01:07.426
Use readiness checks to decide whether learners need more examples or more challenge.

14
00:01:07.426 --> 00:01:10.906
Build progression so support fades as competence grows.

15
00:01:10.906 --> 00:01:16.561
These choices respect both working memory limits and the learner's existing knowledge.

16
00:01:16.561 --> 00:01:22.216
The goal is to support novices without trapping experienced learners in unnecessary detail.

17
00:01:22.216 --> 00:01:27.871
This matters in workplace learning, where audiences often include people with mixed experience.

18
00:01:27.871 --> 00:01:39.181
Good design gives beginners a safe path into the material and gives experienced learners a way to engage with the parts that actually stretch their performance.

19
00:01:39.181 --> 00:01:43.096
Adaptation keeps effort productive for more of the audience.
